    "assemble.data.0849": "Assembled Robot Duck",
    "assemble.data.0850": "Robot duck complete machine",
    "assemble.data.0851": "Use the previously assembled machine to perform calibration and inspection in this chapter.",
    "assemble.data.0852": "No new parts are required for this chapter.",
    "assemble.data.0853": "This page provides assembly instruction. Automatic numbering requires the local personal edition of Debug Duck connected to UNO Q.",
    "assemble.data.0854": "The board shape and interface are simple teaching models; the direction, revision and spacing of the actual board need to be checked.",
    "assemble.data.0855": "Complete the Arduino App Lab, Duck OS and Wi-Fi settings according to the manufacturer's instructions, and start the Duck to run the application on your UNO Q.",
    "assemble.data.0856": "This environment provides instruction only. Automatic configuration requires the local personal edition of Debug Duck; manual setup in the device runtime is also available.",
    "assemble.data.0857": "Manually scan single",
    "assemble.data.0858": "Scan the current servo on the running side of the device",
    "assemble.data.0859": "Open your own Duck Runtime and enter Servo setup. Scan all IDs, stop scanning after finding a single one, read the parameters, and then execute Reset Mid according to the instructions of the current running terminal, and keep uninstalling.",
    "assemble.data.0860": "This page does not send hardware commands. Always connect only one; the parameters are confirmed by matching the firmware.",
    "assemble.data.0861": "Write and read the reply core on the device running side",
    "assemble.data.0862": "Fill in the KP and KD that match the firmware in Servo setup, execute Set KpKd; fill in the target ID, execute Change ID, then read the new number and parameters, and confirm that the old number no longer responds.",
    "assemble.data.0863": "Do not copy parameter values ​​from old videos. The neutral command confirmation is different from the zero position calibration after assembly.",
    "assemble.data.0864": "In Duck Runtime, assign IDs 10–14, 20–24 and 30–34 in order. Label each physical servo. Before every change of connections, shut down the robot and disconnect USB and the battery.",
    "assemble.data.0865": "The ID list here is a teaching reference. It does not prove that IDs have been written or that the mechanical zero has been calibrated. Keep the secondary horns on ID30 and ID31. Removing them on ID10, ID20 and ID32 is optional; this tutorial keeps them. Remove the others only at the specified steps. Keep every main horn.",
